# Copy to .env and set for this machine. Not committed.
#
# RPE_DATA_ROOT is the pipeline tree holding Inputs/, Outputs/ and Build Artifacts/.
# It differs per machine and must never be hardcoded in the build code — see
# build/rpe_env.py. Repointing this line is the ONLY change a new machine needs.

# Google Drive is the source for inputs AND outputs (Aaron, 2026-08-31). Drive is
# the copy that is current, because it is the one Aaron works in. Uncomment the
# line for this machine.

# --- Windows (Drive mounted as a letter) ---
RPE_DATA_ROOT=G:\My Drive\Work\RPE Pipeline

# --- Mac (Google Drive for Desktop) ---
# RPE_DATA_ROOT=/Users/<you>/Library/CloudStorage/GoogleDrive-<account>/My Drive/Work/RPE Pipeline

# --- Retired: C:\Data Pipelines\RPE Pipeline (2026-08-31) ---
# The CSI/Cowork local tree, used after the move off OneDrive (2026-07-17). It is
# GONE from the Windows machine: C:\Data Pipelines\ now holds only "Renewals
# Pipeline", a different project with its own Inputs\ and Outputs\ that looks like
# this one at a glance. Named here so it is recognised and refused, not retried.
# If Drive access is ever lost, ask Aaron for the new root.

# --- Optional ---
# Reporting period for a build, YYYY.MM. Normally taken from the output filename's
# <yyyy.mm> tag. A monthly deck's period is NEVER derived from the Executive Summit
# date — summits run twice a year, so that is wrong ten months out of twelve.
# RPE_PERIOD=2026.08
